course: dictionary
lesson: 7716
title: Understanding puberty
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Puberty is a noun. It is the name for a time in life, not a thing you can hold. «Puberty happens at different times for everyone, usually starting between about 8 and 14.» The word "usually" and the words "at different times" tell you that the start is not the same for every child.
explain: The words around puberty explain it. «Between about 8 and 14, the body starts to change from a child's body to an adult's; this is called puberty.» The phrase "this is called" points straight at the word, so the change in the body is what puberty means.
explain: Puberty is uncountable, so we never say "a puberty" or "puberties". We say «go through puberty», «reach puberty», «start puberty» or «during puberty». Try the swap check: "during a puberty" sounds wrong, so the phrase without "a" is correct.
explain: The sentence «it is caused by hormones» gives you the cause. Hormones are natural chemicals in the body. When you meet a new health word, look for clues like "this is called", "it is caused by" or "for example" to find its meaning.
fact: Puberty means the time when a child's body slowly changes into an adult's body.
fact: Puberty is caused by hormones, which are natural chemicals in the body.
fact: «Children grow fastest as babies and again during puberty.»
fact: «Around puberty special sweat glands in the armpits switch on.» Their sweat is not smelly until bacteria eat it, which is why a wash helps.
fact: Puberty is uncountable: we say «during puberty», never «during a puberty».
exercise: What does puberty mean? | A kind of sweet food | A type of school test | The day a child is born | *The time when a child's body slowly changes into an adult's
exercise: Which words in «Between about 8 and 14, the body starts to change from a child's body to an adult's; this is called puberty» show that puberty is the name for this change? | adult's | it happens at a different time | Between about 8 and 14 | *this is called
exercise: What causes puberty? | Eating too many sweets | *Hormones, which are natural chemicals in the body | Sunshine on the skin | Learning to read
test: Which is the correct way to write it? | during a puberty | *during puberty | during puberties | at puberties
test: Why does a wash help when sweat glands switch on around puberty? | Because it stops puberty | Because sweat is always very smelly | Because hormones make sweat sweet | *Because sweat only smells once bacteria have eaten it
exam: Maya reads «Children grow fastest as babies and again during puberty.» Which best says what puberty is? | A holiday for parents | A kind of medicine | *A time when the body changes towards an adult's | A time for school trips
